# ZeroOS: multi-generation LRU (MGLRU) picks which pages to swap out better
# than the old LRU on small-memory machines (it is what ChromeOS uses), and
# min_ttl_ms keeps the last second's working set in RAM so the UI never
# thrashes. "w-": skipped quietly on a kernel built without it.
w- /sys/kernel/mm/lru_gen/enabled - - - - y
w- /sys/kernel/mm/lru_gen/min_ttl_ms - - - - 1000
